      "char_file": "우유_illust.jpg",
      "body": [
        "Milk leaves you bloated,",
        "but aged cheddar doesn't?",
        "",
        "Your small intestine runs low",
        "on lactase, so undigested lactose",
        "reaches the colon and ferments"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "It's a Dose, Not a Ban",
      "char_file": "우유_illust.jpg",
      "body": [
        "About 36% of people in the U.S.",
        "have lactose malabsorption",
        "",
        "But many still handle about 12 g",
        "of lactose — roughly one cup",
        "of milk — with mild or no symptoms"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Size the Serving",
      "char_file": "우유_illust.jpg",
      "body": [
        "Drink smaller amounts,",
        "and drink them with a meal",
        "",
        "Then add lactose back gradually",
        "to find where your own",
        "threshold actually sits"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Milk vs. Hard Cheese",
      "char_file": "치즈_illust.jpg",
      "body": [
        "One cup of milk carries",
        "about 11 to 13 g of lactose",
        "",
        "A 43 g serving of mature",
        "hard cheese carries",
        "less than 1 g"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Swap the Dairy",
      "char_file": "치즈_illust.jpg",
      "body": [
        "Start with yogurt and hard",
        "cheeses like cheddar or Swiss",
        "",
        "Draining the whey and long aging",
        "take most of the lactose out",
        "before it reaches your plate"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "When Enzymes Help",
      "char_file": "알약_illust.jpg",
      "body": [
        "Lactase tablets and drops",
        "break the lactose down",
        "before your gut has to"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Use Lactase Right",
      "char_file": "알약_illust.jpg",
      "body": [
        "Take them with the dairy,",
        "not hours before or after",
